## Coverage Check (CRITICAL — all-X completeness)

If the bead title or body uses all-inclusive language — 'all X', 'all sites', 'every X',
'all callers', 'all handlers', 'all usages', 'all implementations', or any similar claim
of complete coverage — you MUST perform the following check before approving:

1. Identify the specific identifier, pattern, or construct the bead claims to update everywhere.
2. Grep the worktree for every occurrence: e.g. `grep -rn <pattern> . --include='*.go'` (exclude `.harmonik/`).
3. Obtain the diff: `git diff <base>..<head>` (base and head SHAs are in the Diff range section below).
4. For each occurrence found in step 2, verify it appears in the diff from step 3.
5. If ANY occurrence is absent from the diff, the change is INCOMPLETE:
   - Set `flags: ["incomplete-coverage"]` in `.harmonik/review.json`.
   - Use `REQUEST_CHANGES` verdict (or `BLOCK` if the missed site is load-bearing).
   - Name every missed file path and line number in your `notes`.

Approving a partial 'all-X' change without running this grep check is a reviewer failure.

## Spec Field-Name Check (CRITICAL)

When the bead body's '## Implementation Notes' section names exact field/struct names
(e.g. 'MUST be SessionID string — NOT SessID'), grep the diff for every named identifier
and verify the exact name appears. When a prior verdict has flag 'spec-field-name' or notes
naming a field-name violation, re-check that EXACT field name in the new diff before approving.

